  "notes": "A compound verb combining ⟦{拭|ふ}く→拭く：04261_fuku⟧ (to wipe) and ⟦{消|け}す→消す：00528_kesu⟧ (to erase/extinguish). Used mainly literally, for wiping writing or marks off a surface; for dispelling doubts or anxiety, ⟦{払拭|ふっしょく}→払拭：09461_fusshoku⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ or {拭|ぬぐ}い{去|さ}る is the usual verb.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{黒板|こくばん}→黒板：02756_kokuban⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{字|じ}→字：01606_ji⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{拭|ふ}き{消|け}す: to wipe the writing off the blackboard\n- ⟦{涙|なみだ}→涙：02235_namida⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{拭|ふ}き{消|け}す: to wipe away tears\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {拭|ぬぐ}い{去|さ}る: to wipe away — similar meaning, slightly more literary\n- ⟦{払拭|ふっしょく}→払拭：09461_fusshoku⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to dispel; to wipe clean — formal Sino-Japanese equivalent\n- {消|け}し{去|さ}る: to erase; to obliterate — emphasizes complete removal\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb (す row). Transitive. Conjugates: {拭|ふ}き{消|け}さない, {拭|ふ}き{消|け}して, {拭|ふ}き{消|け}します.",
